                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "RVQOb",
                  "name": "Page head",
                  "width": 820,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 12,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Ln47W",
                      "name": "Title",
                      "fill": "$ink",
                      "content": "Method",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 30,
                      "fontWeight": "700"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "IEJrJ",
                      "name": "Lead",
                      "fill": "$muted",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "3D-GNOMEᴺᴳ turns chromatin loops and a contact map into an ensemble of 3D structures. It follows the multiscale approach of 3D-GNOME [1, 2]. The loop anchors are placed first and the chromatin between them second. This page follows one job from its inputs to its output.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "eEQNe",
                  "name": "Inputs",
                  "width": 820,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 12,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "EdA84",
                      "name": "Heading",
                      "fill": "$ink",
                      "content": "1. Inputs",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 18,
                      "fontWeight": "700"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "qpVvq",
                      "name": "P",
                      "fill": "#3F3E3B",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A job reads loops, a contact map, gene and enhancer positions, and optionally structural variants. The loops hold the structure together at their anchors. The contact map sets how distance grows with genomic separation and adds contacts between pairs without a loop.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "FYxc5",
                      "name": "Table",
                      "clip": true,
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "fill": "$surface",
                      "cornerRadius": 10,
                      "stroke": "$line",
                      "strokeWidth": 1,
                      "layout": "vertical",
