                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The beads between two anchors start on a compact random coil at the bond targets, and the anchors stay where the anchor phase put them. Simulated annealing [8] moves one bead at a time. A move that lowers the energy is accepted. A move that raises it is accepted with probability exp(-c E_new / (E_old T)), and the temperature T falls by a constant factor each step [1, 9]. A wall rejects any move that brings two beads closer than the excluded volume radius.",
