                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "PNamG",
                  "name": "Ensemble",
                  "width": 820,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 12,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "F8tE7",
                      "name": "Heading",
                      "fill": "$ink",
                      "content": "5. Ensemble and output",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 18,
                      "fontWeight": "700"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "a1cAgW",
                      "name": "P",
                      "fill": "#3F3E3B",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The anchor and chain phases repeat from new random starts, one structure per start. Parts of the region with many loops are similar across structures, and parts with few loops vary more. Each structure is saved as an mmCIF file. The job then computes, for every gene, the 3D distance from its promoter to its nearest enhancer within 1 Mb over all structures, as in enhancer3D [10].",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "nphnb",
                  "name": "Engine",
                  "width": 820,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 12,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "XB1NP",
                      "name": "Heading",
                      "fill": "$ink",
                      "content": "6. Engine",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 18,
                      "fontWeight": "700"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "X4CsL",
                      "name": "P",
                      "fill": "#3F3E3B",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A run is a graph of tasks that grows while it runs, figure 3a. The region task adds one task per chromosome, a chromosome task adds its blocks, and each chromosome gets one anchor fit and one chain task per block. Each stage has its own executor, serial, threaded or batched on the GPU. Results are applied in a fixed order, and a run with the same settings and seed gives the same structures.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "BEQx0",
                      "name": "P",
                      "fill": "#3F3E3B",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The chain tasks of many blocks run in one JAX [11] launch on the GPU. Each chain has its own random stream, and the grouping of chains into launches does not change the result of a chain. A chain that converges holds its state while the rest of the launch continues, figure 3b. Each annealing step tests 32 proposals against the current state and applies the first accepted one, which keeps the serial Metropolis rule. Excluded volume uses a grid of cells rebuilt every 2,048 proposals. With several GPUs each launch group goes whole to one GPU, and the output does not depend on the number of GPUs.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
